MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The flap discs felt like a natural next choice after my cutting wheels because finishing and deburring cut parts fits the same work, provided they fit my grinder.",
    "The stainless screws fit my repeated purchases of fastening supplies. Gloves and cut-to-size foam also felt useful for handling messy adhesive projects and cushioning assembled parts, with suitability checked before buying."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament and UV printer resin require a printing setup and project that my purchases do not establish. My tabletop epoxy serves a different purpose, despite also being called resin.",
    "Foam-gun cleaner, brass rods and the emergency switch each solve a specific problem I have not shown a need for. General workshop usefulness is not enough for me to choose them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in DIY supplies seemed to be stretched into an interest in any workshop material, including supplies for equipment I have not shown that I use.",
    "Shared words such as resin and adhesive seemed to count too much, even when the recommended material or cleaner serves a different process."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated fastener purchases and recent cutting wheels point toward assembling, cutting and finishing parts, which makes practical additions to those tasks especially relevant.",
    "Specific sizes, tool compatibility and whether I already have a supply matter to my choices. Another screw pack could help, but only if it fills a gap in my existing assortments."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my fastening and fabrication projects but extended that interest too broadly into specialized supplies without a clear current use."
}
